From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: stop writing 0xceaa into SMHC_FUNS, the silicon does not take it

Why
---
sunxi_mmc_init_host() writes SDXC_CEATA_ON = (0xceaa << 16) into SMHC_FUNS
(offset 0x044) under the comment "Enable CEATA support". Three observations
apply on this controller, and the third is measured:

1. The A733 UM defines only bits 2:0 of SMHC_FUNS -- ABT_RDATA, READ_WAIT,
   HOST_SEND_MMC_IRQRESQ -- with bits 31:3 listed as "/" and a reset value of
   0x0000_0000 (11.3.8.18). There is no magic key and no enable field up there.
2. The string "CEATA" does not appear anywhere in the 1982-page A733 User
   Manual, in V0.92 or in V1.00.
3. The write does not land. Silicon readback on the 8 GiB board, 2026-09-19, with the
   controller pinned awake after a clean HS400 read:

       SMHC2 0x0402_2044 = 0x00010000

   The driver wrote 0xceaa0000. The register holds 0x00010000. The upper bits
   do not latch, so whatever those bits are, they are not a 0xceaa key.

The A733 vendor BSP has this line and keeps it commented out.

What it changes
---------------
Deletes the write and the now-unused SDXC_CEATA_ON definition. The three
documented bits keep their reset values, which is what they already had: the
write only ever set bits the UM does not define, and CE-ATA is not a mode this
tree uses or intends to use.

Scope of the claim
------------------
No performance claim. This removes an undocumented write and does not fix a
measured failure. An undefined write is not a state that can be reasoned about,
and the vendor BSP for this SoC keeps the same line commented out.

Check
-----
0x0402_2044 reads 0x00000000 after boot instead of 0x00010000, and SD and eMMC
keep working: the card enumerates, read and write verify clean. If anything
changes behaviour, the bits were doing something after all.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -285,7 +285,6 @@
 #define SDXC_FIFO_SIZE			16
 
 /* Function select */
-#define SDXC_CEATA_ON			(0xceaa << 16)
 #define SDXC_SEND_IRQ_RESPONSE		BIT(0)
 #define SDXC_SDIO_READ_WAIT		BIT(1)
 #define SDXC_ABORT_READ_DATA		BIT(2)
@@ -596,8 +595,6 @@
 	 * drove it, which is not initialisation.
 	 */
 	mmc_writel(host, REG_A12A, 0);
-	/* Enable CEATA support */
-	mmc_writel(host, REG_FUNS, SDXC_CEATA_ON);
 	/* Set DMA descriptor list base address */
 	mmc_writel(host, REG_DLBA, host->sg_dma >> host->cfg->idma_des_shift);
 
